"chooser" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		Chooser
		<header>A dialog to choose one value from a list, or several.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>The dialog the editor shows when it needs a person to pick from a short list. It's a list of radio buttons (or checkboxes, to pick several), with Cancel and OK, and it hands back what was picked.</>
	<list class="spell-meta">
		<item icon="user">Written for: anyone asking a question in the spell app's editor</>
		<item icon="image">A picture, not live: it's opened by the editor's <text code>editor.choose()</></>
	</>

	<section label="1. What it looks like">
		<icon slot="icon" name="image"/>
		<text paragraph>Over the editor, asked for by <text code>editor.choose()</>: "Pick one" of A, B and C.</>
		<image src="/components/app/_images/Chooser.png" alt="A dialog headed Pick one: a message, three radio buttons A, B and C, then Cancel and OK" appearance="bordered rounded"/>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>A picture, taken by <text code>yarn site:pictures</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Using it">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>Nobody draws it in JSX: ask the editor, with <text code>editor.choose()</>, and wait for the answer. <text code>Actions.choose</> is a button that does, though no toolbar shows one today.</>
		<text paragraph>From code · asking the editor:</>
		<markdown>
			```typescript
			const pick = await editor.choose({ message: "Which deck?", options: ["Red", "Blue"] })
			```
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Call <text code>editor.choose()</> to ask: it needs a <text code>message</> and its options. It opens the chooser with <text code>openChooser()</>, which adds it to the page and takes it away once it's closed.</>
			<item><text code>options</> can be plain values, <text code>&#123; value, text &#125;</> objects, or a map of value to text. The answer is the caller's own value: a number option answers a number.</>
			<item>The answer, once the dialog has gone: OK gives the value picked (with <text code>multiple</>, a list of them); Cancel or Escape gives <text code>undefined</>.</>
			<item><text code>defaultValue</> picks some to start with. Enter anywhere in it is OK; a click outside it does nothing.</>
			<item>It looks like the editor's other dialogs: small, Cancel first. It's a plain list, fine for a handful of options; a long one would want a searchable dropdown.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Props, and where it's drawn">
		<icon slot="icon" name="list check"/>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-api family="Chooser"></>
		</>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>From its code, by <text code>yarn site:data</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>.</>
	</>

